DESCRIPTION:New RCORP line that pays for formalized rural networks to expand regional behavioral-health systems of care through coordinated\, evidence-based SUD prevention\, treatment and recovery services. MORE is an evidence-based SUD/OUD treatment with chronic-pain overlap that network clinicians can be trained in. The most realistic role is training vendor for a rural network applicant\, since only 6 awards are expected and the program is built around networks.\n\nPath: Sub · Priority 11.4\nhttps://simpler.grants.gov/opportunity/02b2d236-f596-4aca-874d-b8e364156ddc
