SUMMARY:[Grant Radar] Baltimore City Opioid Restitution Community Grants Round 2 (FY2027) — cycle watch
DESCRIPTION:This is Baltimore City's own opioid settlement fund (the City did not join the global settlement)\, giving community grants to organizations that treat and support people at overdose risk. A Baltimore treatment or recovery nonprofit could put MORE clinician training into its budget\, either as its own line or with More Therapy as a subcontractor.\n\nPath: Sub · Priority 2.0\nhttps://www.baltimorecity.gov/bcmoor/news/mayors-office-of-overdose-response-and-mayors-office-of-recovery-programs-announce-applications-for-round-two-of-opioid-restitution-fund-community-grants
URL:https://www.baltimorecity.gov/bcmoor/news/mayors-office-of-overdose-response-and-mayors-office-of-recovery-programs-announce-applications-for-round-two-of-opioid-restitution-fund-community-grants
