DTSTAMP:20261030T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
SUMMARY:[Grant Radar] Colorado Opioid Abatement Council Infrastructure Share (next round\, Round 5) — cycle watch
DESCRIPTION:A statewide competitive settlement pool for capital improvements and operational assistance for opioid-abatement infrastructure\, with rural and underserved areas prioritized. MORE fits only as a training line-item inside a ROAC's or provider's project\, for example clinician training tied to a new MOUD or outpatient site (Round 4 funded several).\n\nPath: Line-item · Priority 2.0\nhttps://coag.gov/opioids/colorado-opioid-abatement-council/
URL:https://coag.gov/opioids/colorado-opioid-abatement-council/
