DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270122
SUMMARY:[Grant Radar] Rural Communities Opioid Response Program - Child and Adolescent Behavioral Health (RCORP-CABH) FY2027 — cycle watch
DESCRIPTION:About 9 four-year consortium grants\, up to $1M each\, to set up and expand behavioral health services (MH and SUD) for rural youth aged 5-17. MORE could fit only as a training vendor to a rural consortium if the NOFO allows workforce training and adolescent SUD treatment\; MORE's evidence base is adult\, so the fit is weak.\n\nPath: Sub · Priority 1.0\nhttps://simpler.grants.gov/opportunity/579974eb-28f3-4ba0-8741-fa1a1183cd3e
URL:https://simpler.grants.gov/opportunity/579974eb-28f3-4ba0-8741-fa1a1183cd3e
